  "published": "2025-02-17T10:48:18.923Z",
  "releaseNotes": "## Version 9.3.3 - February 17, 2025\n\n  - **Improved:** Document Viewer:\n    - **Fixed:** \"fileName - string can not be empty\" error when opening some .eml files with the viewer or when converting them to another format.\n      For example, .eml files received from \"Mail Delivery Subsystem\" can contain an attachment without name and content type with \"text/rfc822-headers\"\n      So to prevent the error, \"Untitled attachment.txt\" name will be given to those kind of nameless attachments.\n      Also, in a .eml file, if first part of multipart message was without content-type, it was being treated as an attachment named \"ATT00001.bin\".\n      This attachment's content will now be considered as the body text of the email and it will be removed from the attachments.",
  "requireLicenseAcceptance": false,
  "summary": "File manager control for integrating file browsing, upload & download features into your ASP.NET application or site (WebForms or MVC) rapidly.",
  "title": "ASP.NET File Manager and ASP.NET File Uploader",
  "verbatimVersion": "9.3.3",
